# [S172 Phase-5 D6.1] the incremental flush CHECKPOINT namespace. Run-local
# crash-recovery state, rewritten every PRNG_FLUSH_EVERY survivors — never an
# artifact, never committed. Deliberately separate from the finalizer's
# `.s172_accumulator/`, whose root aliases this checkpoint must not touch.
.s172_checkpoint/

# [S172 Phase-5 D3.5] the finalizer-owned PUBLICATION store — the sibling the
# comment above names. `generations/` holds the immutable chain-authenticated
# generations (each directory named <generation_id>--<sidecar_sha256>, validating
# recursively to a clean-start root); `current` is the atomic pointer swapped at
# publication. The two repo-root NPZ entries are SYMLINKS into it, retargeted on
# every run, so they are POINTERS AND NOT ARTIFACTS: committing one stores a path
# that is stale as soon as the next run swaps `current`, re-dirtying the tree
# every run and meaning nothing in a fresh clone. Under D3.5 the system of record
# for survivor data is the generation chain, not git.
#
# This SUPERSEDES 006623c ("restore bidirectional_survivors_binary.npz to
# tracking — real survivor data, must stay in git"). That ruling was correct for
# what the path was THEN: mode 100644, a regular data file. 46a3828 (D3.5) changed
# what these paths ARE and untracked both in the same commit; .gitignore was never
# updated to match, which is the gap this block closes.
#
# The stale `!bidirectional_survivors_all.npz` negation removed from the block
# above dated from ad5ab8d (2026-03-15), four months before D3.5, and was doubly
# inert: it sat under `*.json`, which cannot match a `.npz`, and it carried a
# trailing `#` comment, which .gitignore treats as part of the pattern.
.s172_accumulator/
bidirectional_survivors_all.npz
bidirectional_survivors_binary.npz

